	url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11054247/},
	doi = {10.1109/USBEREIT65494.2025.11054247},
	abstract = {The article addresses current issues of information security in industrial control systems (ICS) amidst growing threats and increasing complexity of industrial systems. Special attention is given to the analysis of network traffic, its characteristics, and typical scenarios in ICS. The main requirements and recommendations of the Federal Service for Technical and Export Control (FSTEC) in the field of information protection are outlined, including network segmentation, the use of VPNs, data encryption, and access control. Key aspects of traffic monitoring and analysis, such as the examination of specialized protocols, event logging, and anomaly detection, are discussed. The article emphasizes the importance of complying with regulatory requirements and implementing modern security measures to ensure the reliability and safety of critical infrastructure. The integration of advanced technologies, such as artificial intelligence and machine learning, is also highlighted as a means to enhance threat detection and response capabilities. Additionally, the article underscores the need for regular employee training and awareness programs to mitigate risks associated with human error. By adopting a comprehensive approach that combines technical, organizational, and regulatory measures, organizations can strengthen the resilience of their ICS and protect against evolving cyber threats.},
